    logP = 3.5);
  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Isothipendyl is an antihistamine (a phenothiazine-derivative histamine antagonist) used against itching and allergy, applied topically to the skin or taken by mouth. It is not an approved medicine in major markets such as the European Union and is considered investigational, so it is not in widespread clinical use.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q928054\">Wikidata Q928054</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>isothipendyl</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>D04AA22, R06AD09</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=\"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB08802\">DB08802</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=\"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/3781\">3781</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=\"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:135183\">135183</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q928054\">Q928054</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C16H19N3S</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>285.409 g/mol (PubChem CID 3781)</td></tr><tr><td>logP:</td><td>3.5 (Drugs.Common 25.09, not verified)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
